Let MASM settings through gyp-next's MSVS-to-MSBuild conversion.

gyp-next's MASM tool table has exactly one entry:

  _Same(_masm, "UseSafeExceptionHandlers", _boolean)  # /safeseh

and ConvertToMSBuildSettings keeps only settings present in that table.
Anything else takes the else branch, which prints

  Warning: unrecognized setting MASM/PreprocessorDefinitions
  while converting to MSBuild.

and is then never added to the output dictionary. The warning is the only
trace: generation succeeds, the project is written without the setting, and
the build does whatever it does without it.

That is not a harmless omission for an assembler. A .asm source cannot be
selected per configuration -- one generated project holds every configuration
at once -- so a library that needs different assembly per architecture has to
list every variant and have each guard its own body on a define. Which is
precisely what MASM/PreprocessorDefinitions is for, and precisely what cannot
be delivered.

third_party/winwrap is that case. Its redirect table exists twice, as
src/static_redirects.cc for Clang and src/forwarders_{x86,x64}.asm for MSVC,
and the MASM pair guards on WINWRAP_X86 / WINWRAP_X64. Without the define both
files assemble to empty objects, which is not a build failure -- the library
links, exports nothing, and silently does none of what it exists to do. Here
it surfaced one step later, as LNK2001 on the anchor symbol a consumer names
in /INCLUDE:, because that symbol sits inside the same guard.

So this adds the three settings from masm.xml that the table is missing:
PreprocessorDefinitions and IncludePaths, which are /D and /I and have no
substitute, and AdditionalOptions, which ClCompile has for the same reason --
it is the escape hatch that stops the next missing MASM flag needing another
patch.

Nothing is renamed or translated: all three have the same name in MSVS and
MSBuild, so each is a _Same line, in the same shape and alphabetical position
as the ClCompile entries at MSVSSettings.py:580 and :599.

Worth upstreaming rather than carrying. It is additive, it matches the schema
the comment above the table already points at, and the omission looks like
nobody having needed MASM beyond /safeseh rather than a decision.

--- a/tools/gyp-next/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py
+++ b/tools/gyp-next/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py
@@ -1280,4 +1280,7 @@
 # MSBuild MASM settings.
 
 # Options that have the same name in MSVS and MSBuild.
+_Same(_masm, "AdditionalOptions", _string_list)
+_Same(_masm, "IncludePaths", _folder_list)  # /I
+_Same(_masm, "PreprocessorDefinitions", _string_list)  # /D
 _Same(_masm, "UseSafeExceptionHandlers", _boolean)  # /safeseh
